## Fixed — the canonical `userFacingReason` accessor, both inline joins deleted

**The accessor** (`ModelsFetchReport`, `lib/src/providers/models_for_endpoint.dart`) — the reviewer's exact proposal:

```dart
/// The user-facing reason across BOTH answer kinds (gh-1990 review —
/// the single formatting rule, no hand-rolled `message — hint` joins
/// at the call sites): the diagnostic's [reasonText] when the fetch
/// named a failed branch, else the provenance [note] (fallback path,
/// partial filter). Null when neither is present.
String? get userFacingReason => diagnostic == null ? note : reasonText;
```

**Both sites now delegate:**

1. `packages/fa_ui/lib/src/providers/media_slot_picker_page.dart` (~535): `emptyReason = report.userFacingReason;` — the four-line inline ternary is gone.
2. `lib/src/cli/provider_models.dart` `_noteProviderFetchReason` (~948): `final reason = report.userFacingReason;` — the identical inline ternary (which also carried the `note` fallback, i.e. the exact same semantics) is gone.

Behavior-identical today: an empty copilot answer always carries a diagnostic, so the picker page's diagnostic-only path and the accessor agree everywhere it is reachable; the CLI site's semantics are unchanged by construction. Future join drift (prefix, length cap) now has one place to land.

## Fixed — the `/models` body parse is guarded again

**Fix** (`lib/src/providers/models_for_endpoint.dart`): the HTTP-200 handling moved into a dedicated `_modelsReportFrom200(...)` whose FIRST act is the guarded parse:

```dart
final (ModelsEndpointInfo, int, List<(String, String)>, bool)? parsed;
try {
  parsed = _parseCopilotModelsResponse(body);
} on FormatException catch (error) {
  return ModelsFetchReport(
    info: _emptyCopilotInfo,
    diagnostic: ModelsFetchDiagnostic(
      stage: ModelsFetchDiagnostic.stageModels,
      path: path,
      message:
          '$base/models answered an unparseable payload (HTTP 200): $error',
      hint: extraHint,
    ),
  );
}
```

All three contracts restored:

1. **Dialect contract** — a non-JSON HTTP 200 (captive portal / proxy error page / shape drift) answers the empty info with a named diagnostic, never a throw through the dispatch.
2. **AC6/REG** — the legacy `fetchModelsForEndpoint` wraps this same report, so it answers empty instead of throwing (pre-PR behavior).
3. **gh-1990** — the unguarded CLI `/provider copilot` connect flow now gets a named branch instead of a raw `FormatException`; and because the diagnostic keeps `pathFailed: true` (default), the dual-path fallback legitimately RETRIES the other credential route (an individual host may answer what the tenant host doesn't — covered by the new OAuth-path test asserting 2 `/models` attempts + a `models+models` combined stage), while the guarded cache-refresh path classifies it as a fetch reason (`_noteProviderFetchReason` runs — the note no longer vanishes).

**Tests** (`test/providers/copilot_models_diagnostics_test.dart`, RED-first — the OAuth variant reproduced the reviewer's `FormatException` flow before the fix):

- `unparseable HTTP 200 body names its branch — no throw` — fine-grained PAT (single path): stage `models`, message names `unparseable payload … (HTTP 200)`, `pathFailed` true, exactly 1 request.
- `unparseable HTTP 200 body on OAuth retries pat-direct, then names both paths` — the dual-path shape (`stages == ['models', 'models']`).
- `unparseable HTTP 200 body answers empty on the legacy API` — AC6: empty triple, no throw.

Note: the reviewer's literal `final (info, fetchedCount, dropped);` + assignment-in-try snippet is not valid Dart (a pattern variable declaration requires an initializer) — the nullable-record form above is the compiling equivalent.

## Follow-up filed — gh-1990 phase 2: **issue #2003**

https://github.com/IstiN/flutter_agent_harness/issues/2003 — "tier-aware `model_picker_enabled` filter — individual-tier `/models` responses omit the flag, so copilot-IstiN still lists zero models after the phase-1 diagnostics".

The card carries everything the review thread asked to preserve:

- the **one-line class fix** from the implementer guidance (treat ABSENT as selectable when the response comes from the individual host / a no-proxy-ep token; an explicit `false` still drops);
- the **pi-mono parity reference** (`allowPolicyFallback = baseUrl === "https://api.individual.githubcopilot.com"` in `packages/ai/src/auth/oauth/github-copilot.ts` — same trigger, same endpoint scoping);
- the **live-evidence caveat** (the filter path is currently exercised only by synthetic bodies; AC5's `copilot-IstiN` validation names the real branch before the criteria change);
- the requirement that a tier-aware keep keeps phase 1's transparency (a named drop-reason line, not a silent swallow).

No issue existed before this leg — the only `gh-1990` hits were the goal card (#1990) and this PR card (#2001); #2003 is new. AC5 stays open by design until the owner-validation loop runs; this PR ships the diagnostics half.

## Fixed — the combined stage is now documented vocabulary with a programmatic accessor

Chosen shape (option 1, keeping the informative combined value — the existing AC3 test and message wording pin `'exchange+models'` and the string already names both failing paths):

`lib/src/providers/models_for_endpoint.dart`, `ModelsFetchDiagnostic`:

```dart
/// The joiner of a dual-path combined [stage] (`exchange+models`) —
/// the documented extension of the stage vocabulary for the
/// both-credential-paths-failed diagnostic.
static const stageDualJoiner = '+';

/// The individual stages of [stage] — one entry unless the dual-path
/// combined diagnostic named both failing credential paths (then two,
/// e.g. `[stageExchange, stageModels]`). Splitting on the documented
/// [stageDualJoiner] keeps the combined form matchable for consumers.
List<String> get stages => stage.split(stageDualJoiner);
```

The `stage` field doc now states the closed set **and** the combined extension explicitly, so a programmatic consumer matching on the constants has a sanctioned way to handle the dual case (`d.stages.contains(stageExchange)`) without string surgery.

**Test**: the `both paths failing yields the combined reason` AC3 test now additionally asserts `d.stages == ['exchange', 'models']`; the new unparseable-body OAuth test asserts the dual `models+models` form splits through the same accessor.

🚨 **BLOCKING: HTTP 200 with a non-JSON body now THROWS out of the dispatch — the old `on Object → empty` catch was removed with the refactor**

`_parseCopilotModelsResponse(response.body)` runs outside any `try`/`catch` (the only guard left covers the HTTP GET + timeout). Pre-PR, `_CopilotDialect.fetch` wrapped the whole body in `on Object { return empty }`; the refactor moved the parse into `_fetchModelsList` with no equivalent guard. `jsonDecode` at `_parseCopilotModelsResponse` (models_for_endpoint.dart:821) throws `FormatException` on any HTTP 200 whose body is not JSON (captive portal, proxy error page, shape drift on a misconfigured host).

**Verified by execution on this head** (mock client: exchange 200, `/models` 200 with `<html>captive portal</html>`):

```
FormatException: Unexpected character (at character 1)
<html>captive portal</html>
  jsonDecode → _parseCopilotModelsResponse (821:19)
  → _CopilotDialect._fetchModelsList (718:43) → _fetchWithDualPath → fetchReport
```

This breaks three contracts at once:

1. The dialect contract documented at the top of this file: *"Implementations must answer an empty [ModelsEndpointInfo] on any error — the manual-entry fallback in the pickers depends on it."*
2. This PR's own AC6/REG claim ("legacy `fetchModelsForEndpoint` answers are unchanged") — the legacy API throws too, where it never did before.
3. The gh-1990 goal itself: the only caller without a try/catch is the CLI `/provider copilot` connect flow (`_applyCopilotCredentials` → `_fetchProviderModelIds`, provider_commands.dart:895) — a malformed 200 now crashes the interactive flow with a raw exception instead of naming the branch or dropping to manual entry. In the guarded cache-refresh path the throw is caught but misclassified as "dead endpoint" (silently falls back to `[entry.modelId]`) and `_noteProviderFetchReason` is skipped, so the fetch note vanishes exactly in this case.

None of the new tests covers this branch — `'fetchModelsForEndpoint stays empty on failures — no throw'` only pins exchange 401.

**Fix** (and it doubles as another gh-1990 diagnostic branch): wrap the parse, e.g.

```dart
final (info, fetchedCount, dropped);
try {
  (info, fetchedCount, dropped) = _parseCopilotModelsResponse(response.body);
} on FormatException catch (error) {
  return ModelsFetchReport(
    info: _emptyCopilotInfo,
    diagnostic: ModelsFetchDiagnostic(
      stage: ModelsFetchDiagnostic.stageModels,
      path: path,
      message: '$base/models answered an unparseable payload (HTTP 200): $error',
      hint: extraHint,
    ),
  );
}
```

and add the missing test: `fakeCopilot(modelsBody: 'not-json')` → report answers a named diagnostic, legacy API answers empty without throwing.

## Fixed — the embedded exchange body is capped

`lib/src/providers/copilot_oauth.dart` — a single helper feeds all three body-embedding sites (the two 404 branches and the generic non-200 branch):

```dart
/// The response body snippet embedded into the exchange-failure messages
/// (gh-1990 review): capped at 200 chars — the message now reaches five
/// single-line UI surfaces (the CLI `fetch notes:`, the connect sheet,
/// the app model field…), and a misconfigured base URL pointing at an
/// HTML endpoint (or a verbose gateway error page) must not flood them
/// with an unbounded blob.
String _exchangeBodySnippet(String body) {
  final snippet = body.trim();
  return snippet.length > 200 ? '${snippet.substring(0, 200)}…' : snippet;
}
```

**Test** (`test/providers/copilot_test.dart`, RED-first — the unfixed code embedded all 500 chars): `an embedded body is capped for the one-line diagnostics` — a 500-char body on HTTP 429 yields a message containing exactly the first 200 chars and ending with `…` (`contains('x' * 200)`, `isNot(contains('x' * 201))`, `endsWith('…')`). Existing message tests (401/404 wording, tame bodies) stay green — the cap only engages past the budget.

## Fixed — the parser answers the shape; the second decode is gone

Folded into the same change as the parse guard (they share the site): `_parseCopilotModelsResponse` now returns a 4th element — `dataIsList` — so the "empty list vs unexpected shape" distinction is computed in the ONE decode that already had the answer:

```dart
(ModelsEndpointInfo, int, List<(String, String)>, bool) _parseCopilotModelsResponse(String body) {
  final decoded = jsonDecode(body);
  final data = decoded is Map<String, dynamic> ? decoded['data'] : null;
  if (data is! List) {
    return (_emptyCopilotInfo, 0, const <(String, String)>[], false);
  }
  ...
  return ((ids, windows, maxTokens), data.length, dropped, true);
}
```

`_copilotModelsShapeValid` — the second `jsonDecode` of the same body — is **deleted**; `_fetchModelsList`'s empty branch reads the flag the parser returned. Every honest-empty answer now costs one JSON pass instead of two, and the distinction can no longer depend on a re-parse disagreeing with the first decode.

Both `jsonDecode` hazards the thread pointed at are resolved together: the parse is the guarded one (thread 1's `on FormatException` → named diagnostic), and there is exactly one decode site left in the Copilot `/models` path. Existing tests (`an HTTP 200 empty list says the endpoint answered empty`, `an unexpected payload shape is named`) pin both flag outcomes — green unchanged.
